<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="2046fc68">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose of this activity is communicating enough information to the EY project team so that the formal kickoff with
    the client goes smoothly, and work starts in the right direction. Roles and responsibilities of the actual project
    resources and their assigned scope of work are reviewed, adjusted (as necessary) and confirmed. Resource assignment
    should involve a two-way discussion between the PM and the project team. It should gather input from the project team
    concerning their development goals and allow the definition of mutually agreeable performance goals The EY project team
    is oriented to the client, the project and their respective roles in the project. Each EY team member needs to
    understand:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The project plan, communications and other protocols, project governance structure, status reporting, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The client business objectives and the scope of the project (Project Charter)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Their specific role on the project (including performance expectations)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    In addition, in conjunction with the EY team orientation, project administrative protocols are defined and
    communicated.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
